# Freax package sources. One repository per line, Debian-style:
#
#   deb URI SUITE COMPONENT [COMPONENT...]
#
# Freax is single-architecture, so the architecture field is optional and
# every index is binary-all. A URI points at the repository root, which
# has this layout:
#
#   <URI>/dists/<SUITE>/Release
#   <URI>/dists/<SUITE>/<COMPONENT>/binary-all/Packages
#   <URI>/pool/<COMPONENT>/<package>_<version>_all.fpkg
#
# Default upstream repository:
deb https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bufka2011/Freax/main/apt freax main
#
# Add mirrors below or drop extra files in /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.list
# using the same deb-line syntax, for example:
#
#   deb http://192.168.1.5:8000/repo freax main
#
# The legacy OS self-updater (`apt sysupdate` / `apt sysupgrade`) reads this
# file differently: it ignores deb lines and uses the first bare URL it finds,
# falling back to the built-in GitHub URL when there is none. Keep this file
# to deb lines only; a bare URL here would override the self-updater default.
# Pass --source=URL to sysupdate/sysupgrade to point at another OS mirror.